80000 	101				nx	nz				(Number of x (distance) and z (depth for rheological calculations))
0	1000000				x0	xf				(modelizated x range)
0	500000	-5000	2000		xmin   xmax     ymin   ymax		(graphic output window)
20000	40000	18000			default ET (if no .EET file)  espcort, espcortsup (for gravity anomaly and rheological calculations when no .CRUST and .UCRUST)
0	0				altmedidaanom (0 for Bouguer anomaly)	alt0 (altitude of  the initial plate position from sea level)
2900	3300	1000	2800	2400	dens(corteza,manto,amb,infill,sedims)	(densities of crust (just for anomaly calculation), mantle, air (water for oceanic flexure), infilling material (only when switch_topoest=1), sediments)
0e1	-0e-15	.0	0e2		Kerosdif, Keroseol, Ksedim, maxprofsed (constants of:  diffusive erosion, continental background erosion rate, water sedimentation and  max. water thickness contributing to sedimentation)
0					Krest					(restoring force constant)
10					dtmemohori				(time between two consecutives horizons)
0	0	5	2		tiempo(inicial, final, tau, dt)		(initial, final, relaxation and viscoelastic-step   times in Ma)
0					boundary conditions			(0: Continuous simetric half-plate. 1: Broken plate.  2: Continuous plate,  3: Free ends,  4: Hunging plate)
0e12	5e12	0e15			tecforce, appshearforce, appmoment (Horizontal tectonic force, applied force and torque as bound. cond. case 1. (left side))
0	0	0			switch_(visc, rheolimit, topoest)	(switches for: viscoelastic model, rheological calculation, load to stay without moving)
0	0	0			switch_(erosed,compactar,mar)		(switches for: erosional-deositional model, compacting(not available),  existence of sea)
0	1	0	0		switch_(calcanom,output,sacarps,sacarfich)(switches for:  calculate gravity anomaly, file output, postscript output(PV-WAVE), graphic output(PV-WAVE))
